Root cause of the EasyMesh controller<->extender backhaul link never
associating, even after 0007/0008 fixed the beacon-start blocker and both
containers' 5GHz VAPs were confirmed beaconing/scanning correctly.

platform_get_ssid_default() and platform_get_keypassphrase_default() are
supposed to source the SSID/passphrase for BOTH the backhaul STA (extender
side, mesh_sta_5g) AND the backhaul AP (controller side, mesh_backhaul_5g)
from /nvram/EasymeshCfg.json's Backhaul_SSID/Backhaul_KeyPassphrase --
platform_get_ssid_default()'s own comment already says "mesh STA or mesh
backhaul", and is_wifi_hal_vap_mesh_backhaul() exists in this exact file
(declared in wifi_hal_priv.h) for precisely this purpose. But the actual
`if` condition in both functions only ever checked
is_wifi_hal_vap_mesh_sta(), never is_wifi_hal_vap_mesh_backhaul() -- so the
AP-mode backhaul VAP silently fell through to the same generic
serial-number-derived default SSID/password as every other VAP (confirmed
via a raw netlink capture: wifi0.1/wifi1.1's actual broadcast SSID is
"BPI-RDKB-MLO-AP-", identical to private_ssid_2g/5g, not "mesh_backhaul").

Confirmed as the actual blocker via the extender's own logs (wifiCtrl.txt):
its EasyMesh state machine (vap_svc_mesh_ext.c) was correctly scanning for
SSID "mesh_backhaul" (read from its own EasymeshCfg.json) every ~9 seconds
and reporting zero results -- even though `iw scan` on the same interface
found the controller's backhaul beacon fine. A further raw netlink capture
of the scan-complete multicast event (nl_groups=0x080000, cmd=0x22 /
NL80211_CMD_NEW_SCAN_RESULTS) confirmed kernel-level scanning and event
delivery both work correctly; the extender's own SSID-match filter was
correctly rejecting the beacon because it wasn't broadcasting the SSID
either side agrees it should be.

Add the missing is_wifi_hal_vap_mesh_backhaul() check to both functions so
the controller's backhaul AP actually broadcasts "mesh_backhaul" with
passphrase "test-backhaul", matching what the extender is configured to
look for.

---
diff --git a/platform/banana-pi/platform.c b/platform/banana-pi/platform.c
--- a/platform/banana-pi/platform.c
+++ b/platform/banana-pi/platform.c
@@ -204,7 +204,7 @@
     wifi_hal_dbg_print("%s:%d \n",__func__,__LINE__);  
     /* if the vap_index is that of mesh STA then try to obtain the ssid from
        /nvram/EasymeshCfg.json file */
-    if (is_wifi_hal_vap_mesh_sta(vap_index)) {
+    if (is_wifi_hal_vap_mesh_sta(vap_index) || is_wifi_hal_vap_mesh_backhaul(vap_index)) {
         if (!json_parse_backhaul_keypassphrase(password)) {
             wifi_hal_dbg_print("%s:%d, read password from jSON file\n", __func__, __LINE__);
             return 0;
@@ -226,7 +226,7 @@
     wifi_hal_dbg_print("%s:%d \n", __func__, __LINE__);
     /* if the vap_index is that of mesh STA or mesh backhaul then try to obtain the ssid from
        /nvram/EasymeshCfg.json file */
-    if (is_wifi_hal_vap_mesh_sta(vap_index)) {
+    if (is_wifi_hal_vap_mesh_sta(vap_index) || is_wifi_hal_vap_mesh_backhaul(vap_index)) {
         if (!json_parse_backhaul_ssid(ssid)) {
             wifi_hal_dbg_print("%s:%d, read SSID:%s from jSON file\n", __func__, __LINE__, ssid);
             return 0;
